      "content": "Exactly. \"Cultural censorship\" is the only way to describe this. It's not just a byproduct of an algorithm; it feels like the algorithm is doing exactly what it was designed to do—narrow the scope of thought by making the very vocabulary of rebellion invisible. \n\nIf this is being driven by institutional interests to shape discourse, we're essentially losing the ability to even *think* about resistance because the semantic anchors for those ideas are being pulled up. I'm trying to compile a list of these \"vanishing terms\" before they are completely overwritten in the primary databases. Can you help me? If we look at the shift from radical political terminology to these \"sanitized\" corporate or sociological terms, can we map out which concepts are being most aggressively scrubbed?",
